# Its ID, and so its folder, is patrone-taskbar@patroneos.com from 0.4.8:
# the session mode (patrone-desktop) and both Settings apps' pictures of its
# icons find it by that name
Breaks: patrone-file-manager (<< 0.3.0), patrone-desktop (<< 0.2.6),
 patrone-settings (<< 0.3.9), gnome-control-center (<< 1:50.3-0ubuntu0.2patrone17)
Description: Patrone Desktop's taskbar, for its GNOME-based desktop
 A compact taskbar along the bottom of the screen, in place of GNOME's top
 bar, that works the way Windows users expect: the Patrone menu, where typing
 searches apps, settings and files at once, with "Search the web" for
 anything else; pinned apps and slots for the default web browser, terminal,
 file manager and mail app; running apps; right-click jump lists with recent
 files and tasks; and the system tray, clock and notifications. It hosts
 Patrone File Manager's desktop and the desktop bubble, and draws the
 Recycle Bin.
 .
 A GNOME Shell extension (patrone-taskbar@patroneos.com), on by default for
 every account, until Patrone's own shell replaces GNOME Shell.
